    "details": "H.Merijn Brand - Tux \\<linux@tux.freedom.nl\\> reports:\n\n> Text::CSV_XS versions before 1.65 have these vulnerabilities listed\n> below.\n>\n> - CVE-2026-110759: parse (): report trailing lone CR, do not store EOF\n>   as 0xFF\n> - CVE-2026-110758: Under allow_whitespace, do not strip beyond field\n>   start\n> - CVE-2026-110757: combine (): decide quoting from the bytes, not the\n>   NV flags\n> - CVE-2026-110756: Flush saved bytes in Combine ()\n> - CVE-2026-110755: Re-use AHEAD with \\\\r instead of copying\n> - CVE-2026-110754: getline (): free the result array when the parse\n>   fails\n> - CVE-2026-110753: Do not free the bound column scalar in\n>   skip_empty_rows\n> - CVE-2026-110752: fragment (): do not size memory by the selector\n>   integers\n",
    "id": "FreeBSD-2026-0521",
